B = [
('Rolls-Royce', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Rolls-Royce, hushed, monumental and hand-built grandeur. Tall formal verticals, long calm unbroken surfaces and a fine bright line drawn along the length of a form, finished with a tiny sculpted silver figure leaning into the wind as a crowning ornament. Mirror-polished stainless metal, slim vertical fluting, deep lustrous paint in claret, midnight blue, silver and black, often two-toned. Interiors in cream, tan and oxblood leather with tight hand stitching, deep wool pile, glossy burr wood veneer with delicate inlay, and tiny pinpoint lights glowing like a night sky overhead. Interlocked double-R monogram in restrained serif lettering. Photography is dim, warm, reverent and quiet, with soft reflections.'),
('Mini', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Mini, tiny, cheeky and endlessly customisable. A compact boxy volume with everything pushed to the corners, short overhangs, big round eyes and a wide friendly grin. Round chrome forms, thin bright frames and a circular winged badge. Saturated colour in tartan red, island blue, racing green, yellow and white, with a contrasting roof in a second colour, bold twin bonnet stripes and a flag-print roof graphic in red, white and blue. Toggle switches, oversized circular dials and playful retro-modern detail. Lettering is simple, rounded and capitalised. Photography is bright, sunny, urban and youthful, full of personality, stickers and mix-and-match combinations.'),
('Land Rover', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Land Rover, rugged, honest and expedition-ready utility. Upright, flat-sided, squared-off forms with bluff faces, flat slab panels and exposed hinges, bolts and rivets. Matt and satin finishes in olive, bronze green, sand, pale grey, poppy red and white, with an oval green badge with gold-edged lettering as the recurring mark. Roof racks, jerry-can style carriers, canvas, webbing, rubber mats and simple round dials carry a worked-hard spirit. Modern versions add clean utilitarian interiors in black plastic, fabric and a bold exposed structural beam look. Photography shows mud, dust, rivers, dunes and wild landscapes in golden light, with vintage press-ad charm.'),
('Volkswagen', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Volkswagen, friendly, honest and gently witty. One smooth continuous curve with a domed top, round eyes and rounded ends, or else a cheerful flat-faced box with a big sliding side and a two-tone split by a white band. Pastel and sun-faded colour in sea blue, coral red, mint, ivory, sunshine yellow and cream, with slim chrome trim and a round blue and white badge showing interlocked letters in a circle. Plain painted metal, simple fabric, big clear dials and little ornament. Graphic advertising uses flat illustrated poster art, generous white space, simple sans-serif headlines and dry understated humour. Photography is airy, sunny and road-trip nostalgic.'),
('BMW', 'Europe', '1970s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of BMW, precise, driver-focused and athletic. A crisp, low, forward-leaning stance with a sharp shoulder line running end to end, a generous glasshouse and a twin rounded-slot motif repeated as a face. A round blue and white quartered badge inside a black ring is the key mark. Tricolour motorsport stripes in light blue, dark blue and red run as thin parallel bands on bodywork and trim. Palette is silver, black, white, deep blue and grey with sparing red. Materials are brushed metal, carbon weave, perforated leather and clean cockpit-style dials angled toward the viewer. Lettering is clean, wide-set grotesque sans-serif. Photography is dynamic, glossy and shot low with motion blur and cool studio reflections.'),
]
